s=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;are in Canada and North America</li></ul><p><strong>Early maple sugar producers</strong></p><ul><li>made holes in the tree trunks</li><li>used hot <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;to heat the sap</li><li>used tree bark to make containers for collection</li><li>sweetened food and drink with sugar</li></ul><p><strong>Today’s maple syrup</strong></p><p><em>The trees</em></p><ul><li>Tree trunks may not have the correct <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;until they have been growing for 40 years.</li><li>The changing temperature and movement of water within the tree produces the sap.</li></ul><p><em>The production</em></p><ul><li>A tap drilled into the trunk and a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;carries the sap into a bucket.</li><li>Large pans of sap called evaporators are heated by means of a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>A lot of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;is produced during the evaporation process.</li><li>‘Sugar sand’ is removed because it makes the syrup look <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;and affects the taste.</li><li>The syrup is ready for use.</li><li>A huge quantity of sap is needed to make a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t4-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;of maple syrup.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-17-academic-listening-4-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c17-t4-l-q1","part_id":"en-c17-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"floor/floors","correct_answer_variants":["floor","floors"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13822_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t4-l-q2","part_id":"en-c17-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"fridge","correct_answer_variants":["fridge"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13822_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t4-l-q3","part_id":"en-c17-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"shirts","correct_answer_variants":["shirts"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourc